      "message": "Instead of rounding `pix_to_bottom_edge` up to a multiple of 2 in `set_pixels_to_frame_edge()`, I think it is clearer and more correct to handle an odd `pix_to_bottom_edge` here.\n\nFor example, I think we can change this statement to:\n\n```\n    const int block_rows \u003d\n        ((x-\u003epix_to_bottom_edge + pd-\u003esubsampling_y) \u003e\u003e pd-\u003esubsampling_y) + block_height;\n```\n\nPlease double check and make sure that this expression is correct when `pix_to_bottom_edge` is negative. Another possible expression would be:\n\n```\n    const int block_rows \u003d\n        (x-\u003epix_to_bottom_edge - pd-\u003esubsampling_y) / (1 \u003c\u003c pd-\u003esubsampling_y) + block_height;\n```\n\nwhich is equivalent to\n\n```\n    const int block_rows \u003d\n        ROUND_POWER_OF_TWO_SIGNED(x-\u003epix_to_bottom_edge, pd-\u003esubsampling_y) + block_height;\n```",
